  "id": "Compound::DB01078 - Gene::483",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Deslanoside and Atp1b3 through a series of binding and functional interactions. Deslanoside is reported to bind to Fxyd2, which is part of the sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase complex, and this complex is involved in the activity of Atp1b3. Additionally, Deslanoside is shown to bind to Atp1b2, which is also part of the same complex, and this binding leads to the binding of Acetyldigitoxin, which in turn binds to Atp1b3. The lowest common ancestors of these interactions are linked to the Agent Affecting Cardiovascular System and Cardenolide Glycoside, suggesting a broader biological context.\n\nThe evidence supports a pathway where Deslanoside may modulate the activity of Atp1b3 through its interaction with Fxyd2 and Atp1b2, which are both components of the sodium-potassium-exchanging ATPase complex. This suggests that Deslanoside could influence Atp1b3 function, potentially through a mechanism involving the regulation of the ATPase complex. The scores from the different paths indicate a consistent pattern of interaction, with varying levels of confidence, but all pointing toward a plausible biological relationship. The mechanism appears to involve the binding of Deslanoside to a target that is part of a larger functional complex, which then leads to the binding of Acetyldigitoxin and ultimately to Atp1b3.",
